 tent with the author instructions' Thursday May 28 cutoff. Abstract regis
 tration is mandatory. Satellite workshop papers are not main-track opport
 unities. ICORE 2026 lists CoRL as Unranked\, not A/A*/B/C. Size L is an e
 ditorial estimate.\nScope: Machine learning for physical robots\, especia
 lly imitation and reinforcement learning\, learned perception and control
 \, robot foundation models\, and learning-based task and motion planning.
  Includes uncertainty\, generalization\, safety\, human-robot interaction
 \, and datasets grounded in manipulation\, navigation\, or locomotion. Ge
 neral ML is relevant when it makes a substantive contribution to robot le
 arning.\nAdditional topics: Computer Vision & Pattern Recognition\, Proba
 bilistic\, Causal & Uncertainty ML\, Human-AI Interaction & Deployment\, 
 Robustness & Safety\, Learning Theory & Statistical Foundations\nScope so
 urces (2026): https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\nScope l
 ast checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://www.corl.org/
LOCATION:Austin\, Texas\, USA
END:VEVENT
